[web/changes/organizer-add-athlete-consent-20261005/05-security-delta.md#C1BA]
1:# Security Delta — organizer-add-athlete-consent-20261005
2:
3:## Trust boundary
4:
5:Authenticated Web/Flutter clients and organizer-submitted email/name are untrusted. Friend/club candidate visibility and roster writes are server-authorized. Player consent is bound to the JWT subject.
6:
7:## Controls
8:
9:| Risk | Control |
10:|---|---|
11:| Cross-tournament candidate enumeration | manager + verified guard; `isManager` for every request; candidate rows scoped by tournament |
12:| Stale/forged friend | exact `ACCEPTED` plus `deletedAt IS NULL` checked in query and write transaction |
13:| Stale/forged club member | community ID read from tournament; `JOINED` membership rechecked transactionally |
14:| Duplicate or already-rostered user | exclude at read; lock/check on write; DB unique constraints where available; capacity lock |
15:| Email account takeover/linking | link only normalized matching `isEmailVerified=true`; unverified/missing account becomes guest; do not disclose account existence |
16:| Guest claim replay | CSPRNG token; persist hash only; expiry; transaction row lock; single-use; require verified account and matching email when supplied; clear claim material on success |
17:| Claim token leakage | never log token/URL, audit only guest/roster IDs; TLS URL; response shows token once only for manual handoff/failure |
18:| Unescaped mail content | encode all dynamic text and URL attributes; reject unsafe schemes; only application base URL + route |
19:| Consent spoofing | route accepts no target user ID; only JWT subject writes self roster row; timestamp once; UI not rendered in organizer list |
20:| ELO bypass | enqueue/apply/replay/manual update gate `isRanked`, nonempty complete rosters, no guest slots, consent `<= completedAt`; admin history excluded intentionally |
21:| Reminder duplicates | atomic row serialization/claim before send across instances; recheck active roster and live ranked tournament before delivery |
22:| PII leakage | candidates expose name/avatar only; response does not echo email/phone; note/email/token omitted from logs |
23:
24:## Data minimization and residual risk
25:
26:Store optional guest contact data only until claim/expiry policy allows removal; compliance owner must confirm retention and notice. Current mail adapter's provider-level idempotency is not confirmed; transaction/row serialization prevents concurrent duplicate sends but cannot promise exactly-once delivery after a process crash between provider acceptance and DB commit.
